WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.270
- She took out her mechanical
pencil, did (clicks tongue),

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.840
and then she just went for it

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.003
and she went over and
just like stabbed me.

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:11.978
(intense music)

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.000
- So the other day I
was scrolling on Twitter

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.060
and I start seeing photo after photo

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.800
of these little gray
dots on people's hands

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.230
and their knees and their feet,

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.680
and even their faces.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.630
It turned out people were sharing

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.670
these permanent marks that only come

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.788
from being stabbed with a pencil.

00:00:28.788 --> 00:00:30.280
This was the first I ever heard of it,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.900
but it seemed like a really common thing

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.800
based off this Twitter post.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.050
And I have a hard time trusting
the internet in general,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.890
but the amount of people who
were responding with oh my god,

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.490
that happened to me too,
here's a picture of it,

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.460
seemed quite substantial.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.210
I decided to ask around
the BuzzFeed office

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.020
to see if this has
happened to anyone here.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.600
And lo and behold,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.690
happened to way more
people than I thought.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.530
- I wanna say it was third grade

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.120
and I dropped a pencil.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.970
And without looking I
went to go pick it up,

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.430
but without me knowing it had
bounced back up on the eraser.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.780
And I kinda met it halfway
and it stabbed me in the hand.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.190
So I did it to myself, technically.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:09.300
But yeah, I went to the nurse's
office and they took it out

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.510
and it's just kinda
been with me ever since.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.390
- I got this in elementary school

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.120
with just a regular pencil.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.150
I'm not even sure what I was doing,

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.660
but I just remember when I stabbed myself.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.290
- I was about 10 and I was doing homework

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.160
and I think it was very
simple math that I was doing,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.110
but I got very annoyed.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.510
And I was laying on the
floor doing my homework

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:35.200
and I threw the pencil down to my leg

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.720
and it wound up stabbing
me right in the thigh.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.260
The mark is pretty dark

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.040
and I thought for awhile
that it was gonna move,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.410
because the pencil really got in there

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.960
and I had to like pull it out.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.960
I thought that maybe
part of it had broken off

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.370
and it was gonna be in my body
and float around somewhere.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.850
But luckily it stayed there,

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.350
but it's also been like 15 years

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.750
and I don't know what to do.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.950
- I got this in middle school

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.720
and it was a very traumatic
moment in my life.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.680
What had happened was I
was just a little kid,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.390
I was probably like 11 years
old minding my own business.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.480
And the girl next to me sitting in class,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.610
it was just middle of class mind you,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.940
she just like turns to me

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.930
and I think I had said something
that she didn't agree with.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:21.150
And she took out her mechanical
pencil, did (clicks tongue),

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.220
and she went over and
just like stabbed me.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.440
And me being me, defended
myself and I was like oh,

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.570
hell no, that's not gonna happen.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:33.450
It totally punctured my
skin and when I recoiled,

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.830
I saw that a bit of the
mechanical pencil, the lead,

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.620
had been stuck to my skin.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.280
And then if you thought
one stab wasn't enough,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.263
she went in for a second
time and she was successful.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.930
- I thought it seemed crazy
that a mark from a pencil

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.560
can stick with a person for a lifetime.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.850
But I did some research,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.450
it turns out that there is a name

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.233
for this specific type of mark.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.200
- I got this lovely pencil
tattoo in middle school.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.800
I was walking through a crowded hallway

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.310
and someone stabbed me.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.700
I don't know who it was, but
now I got this forever tattoo.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.510
- According to Dr. Cameron Rokhsar,

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.040
associate professor of dermatology

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.120
at Mount Sinai Hospital in New York,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.030
he told BuzzFeed News that calling it

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.550
a pencil tattoo is pretty accurate.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.340
He even said that he was stabbed

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.010
at age eight with a pencil

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.300
and 37 years later he still has the mark.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.300
The stabbing leaves graphite particles

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.983
in the dermis layer of the skin.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.430
If you go to a tattoo shop
and they put ink in your skin,

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.140
that also goes into the
dermis layer as well.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.830
- I've had this pencil mark since 2008.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.700
I remember I was in college

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.690
and I was just talking to
the person in the library

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.730
and my friend comes up
and starts talking to me

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.220
and he was sharpening pencils. (laughs)

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.100
And I just see out of the corner of my eye

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.600
like just a pencil coming down
like this towards my hand.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.320
My instinct was just
to move back, so I did.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.780
And he said afterwards that he was

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.600
just pretending to poke me,

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.790
but then I actually moved
my hand into the pencil.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.863
And the mark has been
there since for 11 years.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.490
- [Jake] Now, according to Dr. Rokhsar,

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.610
these pencil tattoos can be
removed with laser treatment,

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.340
but they don't have to be.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.510
- And I thought I got a little piece

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.450
of the lead stuck in there

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.350
'cause it was one of those really skinny.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.040
And I spent like two days
trying to push out the lead,

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.400
But it didn't end up coming out.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.520
- My pencil broke and I
reached down in my backpack

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.430
and I didn't know my pencil was facing up

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:40.040
and I stabbed myself with it.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.960
And I was like, had this
little piece of lead.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.160
I also forgot about it
and so it sealed up.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.250
And then I think like five years later

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.190
I tried to take it out
by getting a razor blade

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.580
and try to cut it open,
but it was too deep.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.834
And so I just kinda left
it and then there it is.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:03.001
(light bright music)

